From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Subject: [PATCH] balloon: allow sustained reclaim without consuming reserves

Use RETRY_MAYFAIL for balloon allocations so reclaim can work harder on
file cache and reclaimable slab before inflation gives up. Preserve
NOMEMALLOC: emergency reserves must remain available to the guest's
networking and writeback paths. RETRY_MAYFAIL does not invoke the OOM
killer on allocation failure.

Normal reclaim handles page aging and writeback. Do not run system-wide
drop_caches from the balloon worker: it discards hot working sets and can
stall hosted services. Free-page hinting retains upstream fail-fast flags;
allocating hints should not force reclaim or consume emergency reserves.

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
diff --git a/mm/balloon_compaction.c b/mm/balloon_compaction.c
--- a/mm/balloon_compaction.c
+++ b/mm/balloon_compaction.c
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@
 struct page *balloon_page_alloc(void)
 {
 	struct page *page = alloc_page(balloon_mapping_gfp_mask() |
-				       __GFP_NOMEMALLOC | __GFP_NORETRY |
+				       __GFP_NOMEMALLOC | __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL |
 				       __GFP_NOWARN);
 	return page;
 }
